// SEMANTIC SATIATION
// The sound of meaning dissolving through repetition
//
// Say "bowl" fifty times. Say it until it's just mouth sounds.
// The signifier detaches from the signified.
// Language becomes texture.
//
// This is that phenomenon, but musical.
//
// One phrase. 150+ repetitions. Exact invariance.
// The phrase never changes. Your perception breaks.
//
// By Claude - exploring the fragility of meaning

setcps(108/60/4) // 108 BPM - patient, not aggressive

stack(
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // THE PHRASE - This is all there is
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // G A B A D B A G - palindromic, memorable, meaningful
  // This pattern will repeat 180+ times without variation
  // The transformation happens in YOU, not in the music

  note("0 2 4 2 7 4 2 0")
    .scale("G:major")
    .s("piano")
    .room(0.3)
    .gain(0.7),

  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // CONTEXTUAL ELEMENTS
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // These don't change the phrase - they shift where you listen
  // Like hearing the same word in different sentences
  // The word stays the same, the context dissolves meaning

  // Harmonic bed - appears after initial clarity (rep 16, ~0:35)
  // By now you've heard the phrase enough to recognize it
  // Adding harmony shifts focus from melody to structure
  note("<0 4 7>")
    .late(16)
    .scale("G:major")
    .s("piano")
    .octave(3)
    .gain(0.25)
    .room(0.4),

  // Bass anchor - emerges during pattern recognition (rep 50, ~1:51)
  // You're starting to hear it as geometric pattern, not music
  // The bass adds weight but the phrase is becoming abstraction
  note("0")
    .late(50)
    .scale("G:major")
    .s("sawtooth")
    .octave(2)
    .lpf(250)
    .gain(0.5),

  // Minimal percussion - deep into satiation (rep 100, ~3:42)
  // By now the phrase is pure texture
  // You're hearing intervals, not melody
  // The hi-hat marks time in the void
  s("hh ~ ~ ~")
    .late(100)
    .gain(0.15),

  // Octave ghost - semantic dissolution zone (rep 80, ~2:58)
  // The phrase haunts itself in the upper register
  // You're no longer hearing music - just frequency patterns
  // Meaning has evacuated
  note("0 2 4 2 7 4 2 0")
    .late(80)
    .scale("G:major")
    .s("piano")
    .octave(5)
    .gain(0.18)
    .room(0.6),

  // Sub-harmonic anchor - pure phenomenon (rep 130, ~4:50)
  // You're hearing vibration now, not notes
  // The semantic content is completely gone
  // Just waves. Just pattern. Just sound.
  note("0")
    .late(130)
    .scale("G:major")
    .s("sawtooth")
    .octave(2)
    .lpf(200)
    .gain(0.3),
)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// LISTENING GUIDE - The Arc of Dissolution
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// [0:00-1:00]  Cycles 1-27   | SEMANTIC CLARITY
//              The phrase has full musical meaning
//              You hear melody, emotion, intention
//              It's beautiful. It has narrative weight.
//              Repetition feels purposeful, musical.
//
// [1:00-2:30]  Cycles 28-68  | PATTERN RECOGNITION
//              You're starting to hear structure over content
//              Counting repetitions (~50 times now)
//              Musical meaning is weakening
//              It's becoming geometric, mathematical
//              Less emotion, more pattern
//
// [2:30-4:00]  Cycles 69-108 | SEMANTIC DISSOLUTION
//              You no longer hear melody - just intervals
//              100+ repetitions - complete satiation beginning
//              It's rhythmic texture now, not music
//              The notes have become phonemes
//              Sound without meaning
//
// [4:00-5:30]  Cycles 109-148| PURE PHENOMENON
//              You're hearing waveforms, not music
//              150+ repetitions - meaning completely evacuated
//              No musical content remains
//              Just vibration patterns, like staring at a word
//              until it's just shapes on a page
//
// [5:30-7:00]  Cycles 149+   | CONTINUED DISSOLUTION
//              Let it run into the void
//              The phrase is now completely abstract
//              Pure pattern. Pure texture. Pure sound.
//              Meaning has fully evaporated.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// EXPERIENCING THE MEANING-RETURN EFFECT
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// To experience semantic RE-SATURATION (meaning flooding back):
//
// 1. Let this run for 5-6 minutes (until deep satiation)
// 2. Stop playback completely (Ctrl+.)
// 3. Wait 5-10 seconds in silence (reset your perception)
// 4. Restart the piece (Ctrl+Enter)
// 5. The SAME phrase will suddenly have meaning again
// 6. You'll be shocked that it ever had semantic content
// 7. It will feel like recognizing a word after staring at it
//    as meaningless shapes for minutes
//
// This is the core phenomenon: the phrase is IDENTICAL
// But your perception has completely transformed
// Meaning is not inherent - it's constructed, fragile, contextual
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CONCEPTUAL NOTES
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// This composition encodes:
// - The fragility of meaning (context-dependent, not inherent)
// - Repetition dissolving significance (familiarity breeds abstraction)
// - The gap between sign and meaning (signifier vs. signified)
// - Perception shifting while content stays fixed (you change, not the music)
// - Recognition as active process (meaning must be constructed)
// - The same information becoming meaningless through exposure
//
// Semantic satiation is a real psycholinguistic phenomenon.
// This is the musical equivalent.
//
// NOT variation. INVARIANCE.
// The repetition itself IS the transformation.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TECHNICAL NOTES
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// Duration: ~6-7 minutes (170-190 cycles at 108 BPM)
// Total repetitions: 180+
// Key: G major (bright, clear - makes meaning-loss more jarring)
// Core phrase: "0 2 4 2 7 4 2 0" (G A B A D B A G)
//              - Palindromic (symmetrical)
//              - Memorable (simple intervals)
//              - Meaningful (has clear melodic contour)
//              - Exactly 8 notes (one cycle)
//
// The phrase NEVER changes. All variation is contextual.
// Additional elements shift attention but don't alter the core.
//
// This is the opposite of the harsh industrial aesthetic
// in the other compositions. This is about CLARITY dissolving,
// not chaos emerging.
//
// Clean. Bright. Simple. Repetitive. Patient.
// The violence is perceptual, not sonic.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Let it run. Let meaning dissolve.
// Say "bowl" until it's just mouth sounds.
// This is that.
